doc:sch-2-sec-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3 Assets and liabilities of the Australian Heritage" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Commission (1) When this Schedule commences, any rights, property or assets that, immediately before that time, were vested in the Australian Heritage Commission are vested in the Commonwealth. (2) When this Schedule commences, the Commonwealth becomes liable to pay and discharge any debts, liabilities or obligations of the Australian Heritage Commission that existed immediately before that time." ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-heritage-council-consequential-and-transitional-provisions-act-2003-sch-2-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 Registration of transfers of land"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies if:  (a) any right, title or interest in particular land vests in the Commonwealth under item 3; and  (b) there is lodged with a land registration official a certificate that:  (i) is signed by the Minister; and  Transitional provisions  Schedule 2  2003            7  (ii) identifies the land; and  (iii) states that the right, title or interest has become vested in the Commonwealth under item 3. (2) The land registration official may:  (a) register the matter in a way that is the same as, or similar to, the way in which dealings in land of that kind are registered; and  (b) deal with, and give effect to, the certificate. (3) A document that appears to be a certificate under subitem (1) is to be taken to be such a certificate, and to have been properly given, unless the contrary is established. (4) In this item: land registration official, in relation to land, means the Registrar of Titles or other proper officer of the State or Territory in which the land is situated." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This item applies if:  (a) any right, title or interest in particular land vests in the Commonwealth under item 3; and  (b) there is lodged with a land registration official a certificate that:  (i) is signed by the Minister; and  Transitional provisions  Schedule 2  2003            7  (ii) identifies the land; and  (iii) states that the right, title or interest has become vested in the Commonwealth under item 3. (2) The land registration official may:  (a) register the matter in a way that is the same as, or similar to, the way in which dealings in land of that kind are registered; and  (b) deal with, and give effect to, the certificate. (3) A document that appears to be a certificate under subitem (1) is to be taken to be such a certificate, and to have been properly given, unless the contrary is established. (4) In this item: land registration official, in relation to land, means the Registrar of Titles or other proper officer of the State or Territory in which the land is situated."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ccc46a3f4f1fe1631c24dadc1446e5fa158627ec77214e3a61d8030879ad2096" ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Registration of transfers of land" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
